=== layout: big-image

@image

![Drosophila complements](repo:prototype/assets/lect06d-x_linked_genes_1/drosophila_chromosome_complements.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C18 | Drosophila complements*

LECT06D, source slide 7 | Replication and division

@speaker-notes

The collars mark centromeres, and the number or letter identifies the chromosome.
Teal on the arms marks heterochromatin. The mitotic Y is almost entirely heterochromatic.
It still carries genes needed for male fertility. The amount of X heterochromatin varies
among fly stocks.

In male meiosis I, ribosomal DNA (rDNA) in the X heterochromatin pairs with rDNA on
the short arm of the Y. The two centromeres orient toward opposite spindle poles.

